      "writtenOn": "2025-01-07T15:19:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if we need to track this information. I like the idea of using the `RenderImmediateConstants` and `ComputeImmediateConstants` with the embedded user immediates but the trackers know where to set the data without the layout and ImmediateConstant structs.\n\nFor example `CommonImmediateConstantsTrackerBase::SetImmediateData` knows there is the `commonConstants` member and can calculate bit ranges, same for the other functions like `RenderImmediateConstantsTrackerBase::SetClampFragDepth` can do offsetof(RenderImmediateConstants, minClampFragDepth) and pass that to a function that sets the data and can calculate the index from the offset.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "2c9b3767f8260794990afa19a3659731bd416739",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
