      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T02:22:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmmm... This should be good. But I really love the way to use operator -\u003e() to update contents. In that way we don\u0027t worry about offsets and could ensure we place the data in the right place(I think ?) which avoid some potential size issue (like float).\n\nAnd in the final uploading phase, we need to call real graphics APIs which upload a range. I think maybe including non-dirty data to ensure uploading range is as large as possible to reduce the graphics API call could be more optimal.(So, that\u0027s the reason why a make all block dirty if any of them is diry) WDYT?",
